  "term": "ADC",
  "definition": "ADC refers to the CDISC version of the Alzheimer’s Disease Assessment Scale–Cognitive, a summary measure made up of 15 higher-level cognitive tests. It was created by combining Alzheimer’s disease cognitive test content seen across multiple clinical trial forms and the ADNI observational study form.",
